  "notes": "Four round rods (r = 1.148 r₀, r₀ = 3.45 mm) with U ± V cos Ωt at 1 MHz, chosen so m = 100 u sits inside the tip of the first stability region (a ≈ 0.20, q ≈ 0.69): the planar array is the cross-section, and the ions start moving along z (out of the plane) at 5 eV, so the trajectories are their transverse motion over 60 µs. Mass 100 stays near the axis; 88 and 112 are thrown onto the rods within a few RF cycles. Tools › Trap analysis gives a and q for the species set under Bench settings (change the mass there to see each). Lower the DC (the ±12.64 V) to widen the pass band until all three come through; raise it to 14 V and even 100 is lost."
